sub_0201B6C8 (unk_0201B4E8.s) is SysTask_GetData: `ldr r0, [r0, #0x10]`.
text.c declares it `(void)` and calls it with no argument; the ROM's mwcc code
works because r0 still holds UNK_021C5714[textPrinterNumber] from the NULL
check above it. Under the typed wasm bridge a zero-argument call passes r0 = 0,
the printer pointer read from [0x10] was garbage, and Heap_Free of it broke
heap 0's free list (the hang at ov59's first list menu, found with a hardware
watchpoint on the list head). The call passes the task explicitly, which is
the ROM's own r0. render_window.c and unk_020051F4.c already declare it
(SysTask *).

--- a/text.c
+++ b/text.c
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
 u16 UNK_021C5712;
 u8 UNK_021C570C;
 
-extern struct TextPrinter *sub_0201B6C8(void);
+extern struct TextPrinter *sub_0201B6C8(SysTask *);
 
 extern void sub_0201C1A8(struct TextPrinter *printer);
 
@@ -56,7 +56,7 @@
     if (UNK_021C5714[textPrinterNumber] == NULL) {
         return;
     }
-    struct TextPrinter *printer = sub_0201B6C8();
+    struct TextPrinter *printer = sub_0201B6C8(UNK_021C5714[textPrinterNumber]);
     if (printer) {
         sub_0201C238(printer);
         Heap_Free((void *)printer);
